      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T10:15:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand correctly, the `bind` boolean was useless as we can use `p_ccb_bind` value to check if the bcb was bound.\n\n`p_ccb` is never null here otherwise we would have a crash in the  `if (p_ccb-\u003ep_bcb \u003d\u003d p_bcb)` line 187, so the `|| !p_ccb_bind` condition line 201 in the previous version was never true because we were always going in the `if (!bind)` condition just above.\n\nSo, again if I understand correctly, this is way cleaner but doesn\u0027t change any behavior, right?",
